>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC`

``` hol4
Refute.REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC : config -> Abbrev.tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Searches for a counterexample under an exact configuration.

`REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC cfg` calls `Refute.refute_goal cfg` on the supplied
goal.  It uses exactly `cfg` and never consults `Refute.the_config`, so
its behaviour does not depend on the session's interactive defaults.
This is the preferred form for reproducible tools and regression tests,
where the fixed `upd_size` and `upd_card` bounds are usually wanted as
well; `Refute.REFUTE_TAC_WITH` is the convenience form that updates the
interactive configuration for one call instead.

``` hol4
REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC
  (default_config
     |> upd_search (Only [Narrowing])
     |> upd_size 7)
```

Like every Refute tactic, it prints its `Counterexample`,
`NoCounterexample`, or `Unknown` report and then applies `ALL_TAC`,
leaving the goal unchanged in every case.  It honours every field of
`cfg`, including `quiet` and `expect`.

### Failure

A mismatch with a non-default `expect` field raises a HOL error.
Interrupts are re-raised.  Ordinary Refute outcomes do not make the
tactic fail.

